# Set ONE OR MORE of the provider keys below. The app auto-detects every
# key that's present, in this priority order: Google, OpenAI, Anthropic,
# then the generic OpenAI-compatible option. If you set more than one,
# a scan that gets rate-limited on the first provider automatically fails
# over to the next one instead of failing outright — useful if you're on
# free-tier keys. All four support the image input the scanner needs.
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your key(s).

# --- Option 1: Google Gemini (recommended — free tier available) ---------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# --- Option 2: OpenAI --------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Option 3: Anthropic (Claude) --------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-5-haiku-20241022

# --- Option 4: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint --------------------------
# For providers like Groq, OpenRouter, together.ai, a self-hosted vLLM, etc.
# Both the key and base URL are required if you use this option.
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
